    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>30</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>This module acts as a hierarchical 259-to-1 multiplexer tree that bridges sentence memory with the parameter ROM. By partitioning the 9-bit loop address into an 
upper 3-bit zone routing chunk and a lower bit sub-index, the network dynamically extracts the exact 1-bit presence flag for the active feature slot.

This single-bit output serves as the master enable signal for the downstream inference engines, instantly gating model weights so that only features actively present 
in the scanned sentence contribute to the final mathematical accumulation.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="-140" y="-500"/>
    </visualElement>
